{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule","id":1483250,"title":"[V5] I dislike Touchstones as written and am considering a house rule","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-06T13:54:48-07:00","id":1483250,"title":"[V5] I dislike Touchstones as written and am considering a house rule","content":"I know that some of you also had their problems with the way Humanity, Convictions, and Touchstones work in V5, so I come to you with this issue in the hope of getting some advice.<br /> <br /> In general, I like the system well enough. (It's not as good as VtR 2e, but still...) My biggest problem is that Touchstones don't really bring an advantage to the table; actually, they are only liabilities for the PCs, since the damaging or the loss of Touchstones can cause Stains. In fact, they are only relevant because they are loosely tied to Convictions mechanically. So, neither do they bring a narrative advantage to the gameplay, nor do they give the PCs any mechanical benefits.<br /> <br /> (I also think that the Stain-reducing effect of Convictions isn't really a big draw, since it's just as likely that Convictions will force a PC to behave in a disadvantageous way. But this is neither here nor there.)<br /> <br /> As a consequence, I feel the optimal approach to character generation is to take the absolute minimum of Touchstones and thus Convictions... which is kinda sad, to be honest, since I like the general idea that Kindred have to be anchored to humanity in some way, that they need regular reminders of what it meant to be human.<br /> <br /> Anyway, since we haven't actually played V5 yet and are a bit cautious about installing too many house rules before testing the system, I was thinking about a minimally invasive house rule to solve my dissatisfaction with Touchstones:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>&quot;If a PC has engaged with a Touchstone in a meaningful way, then the PC may add 2 dice to their Remorse roll at the end of the session.&quot;</i></b> (This engagement doesn't mean that the PC and the Touchstone must interact, but the player should describe in some detail how the Touchstone helps the PC feel remorseful and more alive.)<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea is to actually use Touchstones as roleplaying opportunities for players that then result in a clear mechanical benefit. Think of Touchstones as a way for getting Remorse stunt dice (to borrow from Exalted for a second). What do you think about this house rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 06-06-2022, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T14:40:55-07:00","id":1483254,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of Touchstones is interesting, but doesn't actually amount to much in the vast, vast majority of games. In the vast majority of games, the ST is trying to tell a story that is part fancy party mean girl socializing, part detective work, part mafia coverup, and part kicking ass with your cool vampire superpowers. He or she doesn't really have time to do much with Touchstones, and even the creative ones don't generally have the creativity to do much with the 12 touchstones of 4 players.<br /> <br /> Touchstones have, consequently, become one of those ideas that are almost irrelevant. People fill them out that part of the sheet, and then promptly forget all about it after getting engrossed in the mean girl socializing, detective work, mafia coverups, and fighting that characterize the vast majority of games.<br /> <br /> I don't know if a simple mechanical change would alter that dynamic, because it's a dynamic rooted in the fact that ST's are not professional writers, and players are not professional improve actors. There is no mechanic that's going to change that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T15:24:21-07:00","id":1483257,"title":"","content":"Sorry for sounding thick, but isn't the touchstone being a liability part of the point? <br /> <br /> Aren't they supposed to be something you always have to keep in mind and stay in contact with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T16:54:14-07:00","id":1483261,"title":"","content":"If you're starting with CofD 2e style ones? Not really.<br /> <br /> In the CofD 2e Touchstones are, generally, positive things to have, even if like many external positive assets you can be harmed indirectly through them. The writing and rules treat Touchstones as things vampires want to have, and makes them worth fighting for. Purposefully wanting to off your own Touchstones makes no sense in a VtR 2e context.<br /> <br /> V5 is written much more from the perspective that Touchstones are liability that's only worth it if you struggle with the Chronicle Tenets. The corebook literal gives killing your own Touchstone because you're tried of the hassle as an example of the mechanics for how Touchstone damage/loss turns into Stains.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> I think there's two things to do with Touchstones in V5:<br /> <br /> 1) Detach Touchstones from specific Convictions, make Touchstones easier replace, and make them less restrictive on what they can be. Yes that's not one &quot;thing&quot; but it's part of a overall effort to make them easier to integrate into the story because it's easier to make ones that are relevant to the kind of story you want to play. Non-human Touchstones are esp. useful for creating relevant ones that don't get in the way of a lot of playstyles.<br /> <br /> 2) Increase their role in Willpower damage recovery (they do have this in VtR 2e and V5, but it's frequently overlooked because it's not a huge bonus in V5). This is can easily be more useful to than the bonus to Remorse rolls (but that's not bad to have too), because V5 uses Willpower damage, a lot, in certain parts of the system (particularly social conflicts).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T19:18:58-07:00","id":1483267,"title":"","content":"The irony is that Touchstones get far more use in Sabbat games than in Camarilla games. In a Sabbat games, Touchstones are these hugely valuable soft targets. Grab a Touchstone, add it to a vozhd, and you've caused Cammies to get sloppy militarily and likely made them frenzy in whatever location they first heard about it, and often caused them to move closer to becoming wights. And the Touchstones themselves aren't generally in on the masquerade, which greatly limits how well they can be defended. This makes them an excellent way to damage Cammy elders who are otherwise heavily protected. Slowly building Touchy the Touchstone-Vozhd can be the focus of months of satisfying gameplay.<br /> <br /> But in a Cammy game?<br /> ST-&quot;The footsteps of the dreaded Vozhd shake the earth! Covering its flesh like huge boils or pimples are the heads of dozens of humans, each crying and their mouths screaming silently as they no longer have lungs. Your heart sinks into your stomach as you realize one of the heads is...BOB SMITH!&quot;<br /> <br /> Player-&quot;Who?&quot;<br /> <br /> ST-&quot;Bob Smith, the hairdresser you made one of your Touchstones&quot;<br /> <br /> Player- *gets a puzzled expression as they haven't looked at that part of their sheet since they made it four months ago* &quot;OH! OH RIGHT! Yeah....okay, I'm like, 'oh no, poor Bob'&quot;<br /> <br /> Okay, I'm being a little hyperbolic, but not by much. There's such long stretches of the game being about fancy parties, detective work, and fighting, that long stretches go by with only minimal contact with their Touchstones, to the point that Touchstones are very much an afterthought. The game simply isn't about Touchstones, yet their function suggests it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T19:31:57-07:00","id":1483268,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that, again as a matter of at presentation at a minimum, that one of the reasons the above example isn't as hyperbolic as it might sound on its face, is that V5 core actively encourages STs to use Touchstones as &quot;damsel in distress&quot; NPCs to create drama and conflict. V5 tells players to expect this sort of use of Touchstones as characters to be stuffed in a fridge, and thus a lot of people are pron to valuing them less. It's hard to get invested in an NPC that's only there to die/etc.in a fashion to push your PC into the plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T19:55:53-07:00","id":1483269,"title":"","content":"I have not been impressed with seeming supplement after supplement including &quot;threaten the characters by their Touchstones&quot; as ST advice, no, like the game itself can't think of any reason for them to exist beyond a punishment mechanism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry for sounding thick, but isn't the touchstone being a liability part of the point?<br /> <br /> Aren't they supposed to be something you always have to keep in mind and stay in contact with? </div> </div> </div>If the game can't of itself invest you in one of its purportedly core ideas/emphases without dipping heavily into a well of negative reinforcement, it's not great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 06-06-2022, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T20:20:05-07:00","id":1483271,"title":"","content":"I think Touchstones are meant to be a narrative tool to help roleplayers who are new to the concept of Vampire: The Masquerade and incentivize human connections.<br /> <br /> <b>HOW I WOULD EXPLAIN TOUCHSTONES</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Your vampire does not have 100% only contact with his fellow vampires. Somewhere, somehow, you have at least one human being that has some emotional value to you. It can be your daughter, your mother, your girlfriend, or some guy that you hate SO MUCH you remember what it's like to be human. These connections are something that makes your vampire feel alive from. The Player, not the ST, should develop them and they should feel like someone that they are invested in roleplaying with. Even if it's just, 'My player character pays for Cindy's college because he's not a deadbeat dad even after death.' Conversely, the ST shouldn't make them a target right out the gate like Lois Lane to Superman. The best use of a Touchstone is not to kill them or threaten them but let them be used as props for the PC to act against in scenes that they want to play out.&quot;<br /> <br /> I actually recommend the ST encourage the player to play both Touchstone AND vampire. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-06-2022, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T20:31:33-07:00","id":1483272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483254#post1483254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea of Touchstones is interesting, but doesn't actually amount to much in the vast, vast majority of games. In the vast majority of games, the ST is trying to tell a story that is part fancy party mean girl socializing, part detective work, part mafia coverup, and part kicking ass with your cool vampire superpowers. He or she doesn't really have time to do much with Touchstones, and even the creative ones don't generally have the creativity to do much with the 12 touchstones of 4 players.<br /> <br /> Touchstones have, consequently, become one of those ideas that are almost irrelevant. People fill them out that part of the sheet, and then promptly forget all about it after getting engrossed in the mean girl socializing, detective work, mafia coverups, and fighting that characterize the vast majority of games.<br /> <br /> I don't know if a simple mechanical change would alter that dynamic, because it's a dynamic rooted in the fact that ST's are not professional writers, and players are not professional improve actors. There is no mechanic that's going to change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there has always been a split between groups where the Riddle plays a big role and those where it's irrelevant. In the chronicles that I GMed, Humanity and the Beast always played important parts. (That's actually one of the reason why V5 brought me back to VtM after many years; I felt that V5 codified a lot of things that I tried to do with my old house rules.)<br /> <br /> Well, my experience playing Exalted was giving a mechanical benefit for elaborate descriptions actually works surprisingly well for players getting invested more. If Touchstones are only there to punish the PCs, it'll incentivize players to ignore them. On the other hand, if they can get a clear mechanical bonus for basically describing one of those &quot;melancholic music moments at the end of a TV episode&quot;, I feel like they will take up the offer.<br /> <br /> So, in essence, I want players to actively bring up their PCs' Touchstones in-game, so these Touchstones can become meaningful to them. Then, when I actually do use the Touchstones as a damsel in distress, the players will at least care about it. That's my hope at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T20:35:52-07:00","id":1483274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483261#post1483261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's two things to do with Touchstones in V5:<br /> <br /> 1) Detach Touchstones from specific Convictions, make Touchstones easier replace, and make them less restrictive on what they can be. Yes that's not one &quot;thing&quot; but it's part of a overall effort to make them easier to integrate into the story because it's easier to make ones that are relevant to the kind of story you want to play. Non-human Touchstones are esp. useful for creating relevant ones that don't get in the way of a lot of playstyles.<br /> <br /> 2) Increase their role in Willpower damage recovery (they do have this in VtR 2e and V5, but it's frequently overlooked because it's not a huge bonus in V5). This is can easily be more useful to than the bonus to Remorse rolls (but that's not bad to have too), because V5 uses Willpower damage, a lot, in certain parts of the system (particularly social conflicts).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like both of these ideas!<br /> <br /> Do you think it would impact the rules in any significant way if I were to implement them as well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T22:06:47-07:00","id":1483281,"title":"","content":"I find that touchstones add a lot during character creation because it makes the player think about how the character would interact with other persons, and is created less into a void.<br /> <br /> How relevant they are in the story depends on what kind of game you run, if it\u2019s constant troupe troubleshooting with 4-6 players, then they are on the back lines. If it is less about chasing a story and more about night to night existence, or just fewer players, I feel they get to the forefront. Not all of them, some are better written or simply fit better.<br /> <br /> These are also characters who may have life skills, and just like they can make unlife interesting for the Kindred, the reverse is also true. Probably somewhere between contacts and Allie\u2019s, and you get them for free - albeit with a heavy cost if something goes wrong.<br /> <br /> A bonus on remorse rolls if spending time roleplaying with a Touchstone sounds like a good thing. But I would vary the bonus depending on how good the scene turns out, possibly and/or what kind of sacrifice the Kindred makes.<br /> <br /> I totally agree that using them as constant damsel in distress quickly removes any attachment and makes them a liability instead.<br /> <br /> I did play around with an idea for touchstones after reasing VTR, but for Revised. I wanted three types, a vulnerable one, easily harmed. This could be a person or a location that the vampire attached to. A more solid foundation, such as another Kindred, a style/subculture that was harder to affect. And finally something like a conviction, a city, a historic figure that was basically impossible to shift. <br /> The more exposed the touchstone was, the more powerful impact (don\u2019t remember by what, lost notes) it had, allowing player to create their own risk and attachments.<br /> I think V5 handles changing Touchstones from a living person just fine. I see why they wanted it like that, but it is a very modular system by design and is in my opinion one of the easiest system to house rule in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T23:12:10-07:00","id":1483287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483274#post1483274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like both of these ideas!<br /> <br /> Do you think it would impact the rules in any significant way if I were to implement them as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you liked them, and no I don't think there should be any issue with using those two ideas and your bonus to Remorse checks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T02:31:23-07:00","id":1483294,"title":"","content":"They remind me a lot of Wraith the oblivion mechanics as does v5 in general. My biggest issue is they're more of a liability than asset in larger games and when I ran v5 for 6 players they quickly bogged the game down. Its also worth noting they'd be the first thing that you'd target in setting. The Sabbat would have a field day during a siege if they do any Intel before attack.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of v5-great concept needed more refinement.<br /> <br /> I've actually implemented them as background merit in my v20 games and allowed for more abstract concepts to be utilised. Rather than being reliant on it for humanity, it simply bolsters it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-07-2022, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T05:16:33-07:00","id":1483303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483294#post1483294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They remind me a lot of Wraith the oblivion mechanics as does v5 in general. My biggest issue is they're more of a liability than asset in larger games and when I ran v5 for 6 players they quickly bogged the game down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Like much of Wraith, the Touchstone mechanic feels too ambitious for a game ordinary people play once a week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483294#post1483294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its also worth noting they'd be the first thing that you'd target in setting. The Sabbat would have a field day during a siege if they do any Intel before attack.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I can definitely confirm that as someone who runs/plays in Sabbat games. Touchstones are prime targets because they are, of necessity, very poorly guarded, and the high frenzy risk and stains that result from their destruction are so damaging to Cammies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-07-2022, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T07:49:54-07:00","id":1483311,"title":"","content":"I agree that Touchstones don't bring enough advantages. Outside of recovering aggravated willpower, there is little reason to interact with them. It doesn't help that many STs are just concerned with telling their own story and forgetting about each character's.<ul><li>Giving Touchstones a bonus for recovering WP seems great, it mechanically incentivize interaction.</li> <li>2 bonus remorse dice seems a bit much, remember that every bonus remorse die halves the chance you lose humanity. You always roll 1 minimum, and so it'd mean the chance of losing humanity is 12,5%. Though, interacting with Touchstones means they are more vulnerable, so it may balance itself out.</li> </ul>Most vampires only have 1 touchstone anyway, with 2 being outliers and 3 being extremely rare. Even my characters barely ever have more than 1, as I like characters more disconnected from humanity, and at greater risk of degenerating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T08:17:41-07:00","id":1483312,"title":"","content":"I have not tested it, but a friend gave me an idea about this. Instead of recover each session automatically your composure/resolve in willpower yo don't recover it until you interact in some meaningfull way with a touchstone. This will give to the players incentives to search for their touchstones and involve them in their night to night. What do you think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25915-nicolai","name":"nicolai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T11:19:06-07:00","id":1483320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483311#post1483311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that Touchstones don't bring enough advantages. Outside of recovering aggravated willpower, there is little reason to interact with them. It doesn't help that many STs are just concerned with telling their own story and forgetting about each character's.<ul><li>Giving Touchstones a bonus for recovering WP seems great, it mechanically incentivize interaction.</li> <li>2 bonus remorse dice seems a bit much, remember that every bonus remorse die halves the chance you lose humanity. You always roll 1 minimum, and so it'd mean the chance of losing humanity is 12,5%. Though, interacting with Touchstones means they are more vulnerable, so it may balance itself out.</li> </ul>Most vampires only have 1 touchstone anyway, with 2 being outliers and 3 being extremely rare. Even my characters barely ever have more than 1, as I like characters more disconnected from humanity, and at greater risk of degenerating.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also easy enough to incentivize by giving XP for it. At the end of a session, award 1XP for playing consistent with a character concept, 1 for hunting consistent with your predator type, 1 for actively pursuing your Ambition, and 1 doe interacting meaningfully with your Touchstones.<br /> <br /> I realize that V5 usually gives Willpower recovery as a carrot for this kind of thing, but it XP works too--I have seen this kind of scheme work really well in Blades in the Dark where you get XP for roleplaying in specific ways that are consistent with your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin","name":"Random Goblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T12:01:17-07:00","id":1483323,"title":"","content":"I am biased, because I love Exalted Intimacies, but I think you could drop Convictions and Touchstones as they are written, and make them types of Intimacies (corresponding to what Exalted calls principles and ties, respectively). <br /> <br /> That means they can serve multiple purposes: regaining/healing WP, gaining XP, replacing V5's social combat system, and giving the ST hooks to create story ideas. You can just read Exalted 3e for how Intimacies work, and then adapt them yourself.<br /> <br /> They work sort of like Aspects in Fate, that you leverage to influence others. You can impose new Intimacies on people and weaken or strengthen existing ones too. Uncovering them also adds more to social scenes. WP damage becomes a last resort when you want to refuse influence, rather than the default. They're also great for coming up with ambitions.<br /> <br /> ETA: I snipped a big essay here. If you want more detailed rules, let me know, as it was looooong! I did save my original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-07-2022, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T12:05:50-07:00","id":1483324,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27061_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27061\" data-vbnamecard=\"27061\">Random Goblin</a> <br /> While not a bad idea, one has to consider how that interacts with V5's intended XP rates. V5 gives out XP very slowly, with 1 XP per session the default and 2 XP per session being &quot;fast.&quot; Jumping up to 4/per could easily disrupt other parts of the game if you don't take that into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T12:46:07-07:00","id":1483328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483324#post1483324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27061_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27061\" data-vbnamecard=\"27061\">Random Goblin</a><br /> While not a bad idea, one has to consider how that interacts with V5's intended XP rates. V5 gives out XP very slowly, with 1 XP per session the default and 2 XP per session being &quot;fast.&quot; Jumping up to 4/per could easily disrupt other parts of the game if you don't take that into consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure I agree that it would be disruptive to anything other than the speed of character improvement, which is still going to be slow even with 4 points per session, but if that's the sticking point, then some other variation on the theme would work just as well. My point was just to continue to riff of of the notion that players will do what the game incentivizes them to do, and frequently it is very simple to add some carrots to move the game in the right direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin","name":"Random Goblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T21:22:06-07:00","id":1483438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicolai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483312#post1483312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not tested it, but a friend gave me an idea about this. Instead of recover each session automatically your composure/resolve in willpower yo don't recover it until you interact in some meaningfull way with a touchstone. This will give to the players incentives to search for their touchstones and involve them in their night to night. What do you think about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule of thumb, making the game harder just to have a bonus not be actually a bonus isn't a great design option. Imposing them as a requirement to recover WP will still feel as a hassle instead of a benefit, and risk problems when characters aren't able to do it for any reason.<br /> <br /> Remember, the problem isn't that they don't have mechanics, is that those mechanics feel like a chore, not a benefit.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>' suggestions plus OP's idea work well for starters. Another simple solution is to include them directly in the, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> described, fancy parties, detective work, and fighting. They don't need to be in-the-know or something to be characters with abilities, networks and goals relevant to the game and stakes on the story.<br /> <br /> Making this isn't hard once you reduce the number of Touchstones to a more manageable 1 per player. Basically the players give you a host of NPCs for you to use, just use them. Make one the Mayor's secretary they must go through directly or not from time to time, another may be the city's main gun seller, the last is the coterie's landlord. Now those characters have other roles in the game than just being The Touchstone&quot;, which makes going after them seems less intrusive to the plot even when they are indeed being seek &quot;just&quot; as Touchstones.<br /> <br /> But unfortunately the game never gave any advice on how to do this, it just goes through the &quot;liability&quot; route...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T22:55:08-07:00","id":1483444,"title":"","content":"Something that I don't think is actually against the rules (and thus wouldn't require a house rule per se), but is kinda skipped in V5 while very present in VtR 2e:<br /> <br /> Let players attached other traits to their Touchstones. One very simple way to keep them involved is by having them be things like allies/retainers/mentors/contacts/etc. While perhaps a bit much for VtM to copy directly? Make an Alfred to your Bruce Wayne. Or countless other examples. Comic books inspirations might mean some adjustments to the tone of your V5 game, but they are full of skilled-enough-to-be-useful characters that do double duty as emotional anchors for the main characters they're attached to. Even bright shiny superheros recognize that the stories need some more grounded characters to keep said superheroes feel connected to everyday people.<br /> <br /> This can also make the liability side of things more organic and fun, as the players are designing characters - not mechanical bonuses - that are going to have some natural negatives to them. Lois Lane is a highly talented journalist with a nose for public corruption cases meaning she has contacts, informants, and connections all over one of the biggest and most important cities in the country... and exposing the secrets of powerful people is dangerous in the real world, let alone the WoD, requiring the PC to put in some work to keep her safe. Plus if anyone is concerned that Lois Lane isn't a dark enough example of how abusive being tied to a vampire can be, I invite you to dig into some of the horrific abusive shit Superman did to her during the Golden and Silver ages of comics to justify protecting his dual identity. Pick up any Batman classic graphic novel, and you're probably going to find out about yet another example of how Bruce treats the few people in his life that can actually connect to him as a human being like garbage.<br /> <br /> You do not have to reach far to twist these from purely positive relationships to dysfunctional ones as befits the tone of your chronicle, and you get the added bonus of Touchstones the players want to bring into the story because they paid to have useful NPCs with their dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T04:06:25-07:00","id":1483453,"title":"","content":"Foe referance point in v20 my touchstone background that can be anything you're emotionally invested in at gm's discretion and you ad dice to your conscience rolls per dot.<br /> You make a degeneration rolls if source is destroyed however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T05:15:48-07:00","id":1483455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483268#post1483268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that, again as a matter of at presentation at a minimum, that one of the reasons the above example isn't as hyperbolic as it might sound on its face, is that V5 core actively encourages STs to use Touchstones as &quot;damsel in distress&quot; NPCs to create drama and conflict. V5 tells players to expect this sort of use of Touchstones as characters to be stuffed in a fridge, and thus a lot of people are pron to valuing them less. It's hard to get invested in an NPC that's only there to die/etc.in a fashion to push your PC into the plot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite the same for a long shot, but that kind of makes me remember player reactions in an elders game when the ST asked us about the possibility of childer.<br /> I was pretty much the only one in a group of five not to answer &quot;nope, none&quot; pretty much on reflex.<br /> <br /> Seriously, that seemed so automatic from everybody that it gave me pause and made me say &quot;didn't plan on it, but see no reason against it either - let me get back on that later?&quot;<br /> <br /> (That character ended up having 3 childer, one of them an elder on its own right and quite involved into the chronicle's narrative in fact <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b)<br /> <br /> But yeah, &quot;acquaitances as potential liabilities/targets&quot; is an unfortunately too common fear/trope/vice - and far from unjustifiedly should be said.<br /> That V5's mechanics seems to make that basically <b><i>the whole point of touchstones</i></b>, doesn't help any with giving them any sort of appeal with players - or STs, who have to keep track of the whole bunch of them for questionable payoff.<br /> <br /> And i'm not even speaking of any mechanical benefits whatsoever - but seeing a character connected to your own develop and grow in participation or relevance in the chronicle in ways big or small, can be its own dramatic reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-11-2022, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T12:23:23-07:00","id":1483634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule#post1483250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I like the system well enough. (It's not as good as VtR 2e, but still...) My biggest problem is that Touchstones don't really bring an advantage to the table; actually, they are only liabilities for the PCs, since the damaging or the loss of Touchstones can cause Stains. In fact, they are only relevant because they are loosely tied to Convictions mechanically. So, neither do they bring a narrative advantage to the gameplay, nor do they give the PCs any mechanical benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't play V5 so I can't comment on it per se. But I know that way back when my gaming group first started doing more roleplay oriented stuff - providing backstory to characters, giving them real personalities, having more goals than to just get more gold and XP - there was a bad problem with the GM going &quot;ah, the PC now has a love interest (or a little sibling, or some other loved one) so I can put that character in jeopardy or kidnapped by my NPC villain&quot;. Now if that was only done once in a blue moon, that would be OK. But it quickly became the default move by every GM to every such character.<br /> <br /> The result? All the players STOPPED including such characters in their backgrounds, or building close relationships with NPCs. It was always a detriment that would hijack the game instead of adding fun to the players. So our campaign stopped being as good as it could have been because the ST could only use our contributions in the most negative way against us (I don't blame our GM too much, this is a common mistake by GMs before they have a lot of experience).<br /> <br /> From your description, I can see Touchstones being the same thing. If it can only be used negatively against the PC, players eventually become detached and sullen. There has to be the potential for something positive for the PC to happen.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily think a single, defined mechanical benefit that always applies is the key. It might be. There might be a table of possible benefits the ST (or player) could pick and choose from (perhaps limited by their actual relationship or interaction with the Touchstone). Or maybe it is merely narrative or ST fiat (hey, that was a good scene with your Touchstone, increase your Humanity or eliminate a Stain). But there should be something. The more a Touchstone represents a negative experience (through mechanics or narrative), the more benefit (in some form) it should provide in some way. Otherwise, it's something that is going to become neglected instead of providing for a meaningful and fun roleplay experience (which I assume is the purpose is Touchstones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 06-10-2022, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T21:10:16-07:00","id":1483687,"title":"","content":"I think the mere suggestion of using such NPCs as kidnap targets should be scrapped from the books, it's already easy enough to fall on without that.<br /> <br /> My wife told me about a Mage character of her that had an attachment represented by several Backgrounds and Merits at once, so it was meant to be a really powerful and useful relationship. Basically, her husband was a Rank 3 Silver Fang and Alpha of a Pack. Yet the actual experience, because True Love was one of the <b>Merits</b>, was that this character never appeared in play in any other role than Damsel in Distress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T00:12:10-07:00","id":1483696,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of different Touchstones offering a different benefit. These are entirely unbalanced and untested, but you could have something like this:<br /> <br /> Person - Your Humanity counts as two dots higher for the purposes of using blush of life and blending in among mortals.<br /> Institution - Downgrade one level of aggravated WP damage to superficial if you spend time engaging with your Touchstone. If you spend your daysleep surrounded by the institution, downgrade two levels.<br /> Place - You can downgrade a single level of aggravated damage to superficial per day you sleep in your Touchstone.<br /> Family - As long as your family survives, your Humanity counts as two dots higher for the purposes of rising from torpor.<br /> Ritual - Whenever you spend time engaging in your ritual, you may heal one level of superficial WP damage. If you teach the ritual to someone else, you may heal one level of aggravated WP damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T00:49:04-07:00","id":1483700,"title":"","content":"While I find it a bit depressing that it's somewhat necessary, the CofD 2e Merits include the True Friend Merit. It has enough other mechanics to justify itself and its cost, but any NPC you slap that on is granted plot armor. It is very much a thing you take to say, &quot;No, this character is not for getting kidnapped, attacked, etc.&quot; A True Friend can only be at risk if the player choose to include them in a situation where there's predictable risk that it would cause serious harm to them or the relationship. So if you take your True Friend into a combat scene... they can die, but the ST isn't allowed to kidnap them and use their life to push your PC into acting.<br /> <br /> I'd rather not have to have rules like that, but at the same time it's at least empowering to the player that the option exists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T01:50:44-07:00","id":1483707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483700#post1483700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I find it a bit depressing that it's somewhat necessary, the CofD 2e Merits include the True Friend Merit. It has enough other mechanics to justify itself and its cost, but any NPC you slap that on is granted plot armor. It is very much a thing you take to say, &amp;quot;No, this character is not for getting kidnapped, attacked, etc.&amp;quot; A True Friend can only be at risk if the player choose to include them in a situation where there's predictable risk that it would cause serious harm to them or the relationship. So if you take your True Friend into a combat scene... they can die, but the ST isn't allowed to kidnap them and use their life to push your PC into acting.<br /> <br /> I'd rather not have to have rules like that, but at the same time it's at least empowering to the player that the option exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just make that a free part of being a Touchstone. Then if you want Touchstones to be vulnerable to the whims of the plot, you can choose to make them so, perhaps for some meta reward (WP, XP, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T02:45:31-07:00","id":1483709,"title":"","content":"True Friends don't have to be Touchstones, and as I said, True Friend has a lot of other bonuses than just that. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure it would be a good idea to make that benefit free like that, because it loses a lot of its meaning otherwise. It's putting a significant chit down to say, &quot;this NPC is so important to my view of my PC, that I want as much control over them as my PC.&quot; When for the most part, NPCs are supposed to serve the whims of the plot more than the whims of one player. <br /> <br /> If you want to move to a more default constrained GM mode of play, I'd do something far more holistic and copy games where player actions generate a meta-currency the GM can then spend to do things like put NPCs in distress; then Touchstones can just cost more than NPCs that don't have have any or much other mechanical rating to them.<br /> <br /> IME and IMO, you want to avoid pushing the players and GM from being to antagonistic towards each other with the mechanics. You don't want the ST constantly frustrated because the Touchstones are never brought into anything fun because the players keep citing Touchstone plot armor. Neither side is having fun in that situation. The CofD method is restrictive enough players aren't really going to use it on every NPC they want to have around (and if they do that's a whole big reason to stop and have a chat). The ST can still do stuff they think is going to be fun with half a dozen other characters. The Doom/Tension/etc pool approach is a rules mediated trade off where the players get to exert some control now, for the cost of giving it up later. When the players decide how much ammo to give the ST, they tend to feel more engaged with how things play out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T07:16:41-07:00","id":1483716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483250-v5-i-dislike-touchstones-as-written-and-am-considering-a-house-rule?p=1483709#post1483709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Friends don't have to be Touchstones, and as I said, True Friend has a lot of other bonuses than just that. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure it would be a good idea to make that benefit free like that, because it loses a lot of its meaning otherwise. It's putting a significant chit down to say, &amp;quot;this NPC is so important to my view of my PC, that I want as much control over them as my PC.&amp;quot; When for the most part, NPCs are supposed to serve the whims of the plot more than the whims of one player. <br /> <br /> If you want to move to a more default constrained GM mode of play, I'd do something far more holistic and copy games where player actions generate a meta-currency the GM can then spend to do things like put NPCs in distress; then Touchstones can just cost more than NPCs that don't have have any or much other mechanical rating to them.<br /> <br /> IME and IMO, you want to avoid pushing the players and GM from being to antagonistic towards each other with the mechanics. You don't want the ST constantly frustrated because the Touchstones are never brought into anything fun because the players keep citing Touchstone plot armor. Neither side is having fun in that situation. The CofD method is restrictive enough players aren't really going to use it on every NPC they want to have around (and if they do that's a whole big reason to stop and have a chat). The ST can still do stuff they think is going to be fun with half a dozen other characters. The Doom/Tension/etc pool approach is a rules mediated trade off where the players get to exert some control now, for the cost of giving it up later. When the players decide how much ammo to give the ST, they tend to feel more engaged with how things play out.</div> </div> </div> </div>All good points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T14:39:49-07:00","id":1483747,"title":"","content":"Tonights session had a fun event which relates to the issue of touchstones.<br /> <br /> Carmarilla pc neonates human daughter has gone missing and coterie is investigating, the group is in her room. The nosferatu crits a investigation roll and notices something 'interesting' about the selfies around the daughters mirror. Quite a few of the pictures with her friends have an 18 year girl known to be an infamous lasombra sabbat scout/enforcer. The player was delighted by the absolute horror as she realised just why the gm has been having her shy daughter act more outgoing and socially active over the last 5 sessions. Gm did a great job describing the individual photo's and the sinking sensation of just how long it's being going on and how much of her personal life this lasombra is aware off, she's even visited the toreador primogens nightclub and been in the pc's haven.....lil miss lasombra was even wearing a Korean boy bands hoodie which her daughter had gone to the gig of while sitting on pc's couch in one pic.<br /> <br /> I think it highlights the potential and potential problems of touchstones quite well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-12-2022, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}